title:: BMMultichannelPluginsRack
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - manage multichannel plugins
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMMultichannelPluginsRack manages multichannel plugins (instances of link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPlugin::). It can thus provide a multichannel processing stage at a particular point in an audio chain.

This functions in a similar way to link::Classes/Plugins/BMTrimPluginsRack:: and link::Classes/Plugins/BMTrimPluginsStrip::. The primary difference is that there is only a single 'strip' since the channel inputs and outputs for each plugin are arbitrary. Plugins do execute in the specified order however, so it is possible to chain them by using the output channels of one as the inputs of another.

See also: link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPlugin::, link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPluginSpec::, link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray::, link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractAudioChainElement::, link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPluginsRackGUI::, link::Classes/Plugins/BMTrimPluginsRack::

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Create a new BMMultichannelPluginsRack.

argument:: ins
An instance of link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray:: indicating the input channels which are to be processed.
argument:: outs
An instance of link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMInOutArray:: indicating the available output channels. If nil is passed here the ins will be used as outputs as well.
argument:: target
Target for this object's link::Classes/Group::. If target is not a Group or link::Classes/Synth::, it will be converted as follows: If it is a link::Classes/Server::, it will be converted to the default_group of that server. If it is nil, to the default_group of the default Server. strong::Note::: A Synth is not a valid target for code::\addToHead:: and code::\addToTail::.
argument:: addAction
one of the following Symbols:		
code::\addToHead:: - add at the head of the group specified by strong::target::
code::\addToTail:: - (the default) add at the tail of the group specified by strong::target::
code::\addAfter:: - add immediately after strong::target:: in its server's node order
code::\addBefore:: - add immediately before strong::target:: in its server's node order
code::\addReplace:: - replace strong::target:: and take its place in its server's node order
argument:: name
A link::Classes/Symbol:: indicating the name of this object. If not supplied one will be generated.


INSTANCEMETHODS::
	
method:: plugins
Returns a List of this strip's link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPlugin:: instances in the order in which they execute.
				
				
method:: clear
Remove all plugins from this rack.


method:: mappings
Returns an link::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: containing the current values for each channel for this rack, in the form IdentityDictionary[plugins->[[plugin.spec.name, plugin.inputs, plugin.outputs, plugin.attributes, plugin.values], ...] ]. Subclasses may override this to include additional parameters.


method:: mappings
Set this objects trim and plugin settings.

argument:: dict - An link::Classes/IdentityDictionary:: containing the current values for each channel for this rack, in the form dentityDictionary[plugins->[[plugin.spec.name, plugin.inputs, plugin.outputs, plugin.attributes, plugin.values], ...] ]. Subclasses may override this to include additional parameters.


addPlugin
Add a plugin to this rack, at the end of its chain of plugins.

argument:: plugin
A link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPlugin::.


method:: removePlugin
Remove a plugin from this rack's chain of plugins.

argument:: indexOrPlugin
Either the index of the plugin to remove or the link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPlugin:: itself.


method:: movePluginUp
Move a plugin up one position in this rack's chain of plugins.

argument:: index
The index of the plugin to move.


method:: movePluginDown
Move a plugin down one position in this rack's chain of plugins.

argument:: index
The index of the plugin to move.


method:: free
Free this strip's plugins, group and other resources. After this you should not use this object.


method:: gui
Creates and returns a link::Classes/Plugins/BMMultichannelPluginsRackGUI:: using this as an argument.


Examples::

code::
s.boot;

// 5.1 Array (-0.1)
(
l = [[-30, 'L'], [30, 'R'], [0, 'C'], [-110, 'Ls'], [110, 'Rs']].collectAs({|el, i|
	BMSpeaker.newFromSpherical(el[1], i, el[0], 0, 2);
}, BMInOutArray);
)

b = Bus.audio(s, 1);

x = {Out.ar(b, PinkNoise.ar(0.2))}.play; // something to pan

i = b.asBMInOutArray(\noiseBus);

r = BMMultichannelPluginsRack(i, l, x, \addAfter, 'Plug em In');

r.addPlugin(BMMultichannelPlugin('2D VBAP Auto Panner', i, l));

s.meter;

r.gui; // play with the GUI

x.free; r.free; b.free;
::
